<!--
     Base config.xml defaults max_server_memory_usage_to_ram_ratio to 0.9:
     ClickHouse will try to use up to 90% of whatever RAM it detects on
     the host. Without an explicit container memory limit, that host
     figure isn't "this container's share", it's the VPS's entire RAM;
     ClickHouse alone could crowd out Redpanda, Dagster, and everything
     else. docker-compose.yml now sets a hard container limit (mem_limit)
     as the real safety net; this sets a soft limit somewhat below that
     hard ceiling, so ClickHouse rejects/degrades queries gracefully via
     its own memory tracker instead of getting killed abruptly by the
     Linux OOM killer when it hits the cgroup wall.

     2.5 GiB, under the 3g container mem_limit.
-->
<clickhouse>
    <max_server_memory_usage>2684354560</max_server_memory_usage>
</clickhouse>
